#Sat Oct 24 15:15:00 COT 2026
comment0.target=SlotMachineC4Test
comment0.text=\n The SlotMachine test class for cycle 4\: the different types of wheels\n (normal, lefty, rebel, lazy) and of symbols (normal, ephemeral, shy,\n dizzy). The machine is never made visible, so no window is opened.\n Besides their type and that they keep working as symbols, the behaviour\n of the special symbols (shrinking, hiding, flipping) is verified through\n the Symbol object each wheel shows, obtained with Wheel.getShownSymbol().\n\n @author  Oscar Poveda, Elian Ibarra\n @version 1.0\n
comment1.target=SlotMachineC4Test()
comment1.text=\n Default constructor for test class SlotMachineC4Test\n
comment10.target=void leftyShouldCopyItsLeftNeighborWhenSpun()
comment10.text=\n Verifies that a lefty wheel with a wheel on its left copies the\n symbol that wheel is showing when it is spun.\n
comment11.target=void leftyShouldCopyItsLeftNeighborWhenSpunBySteps()
comment11.text=\n Verifies that a lefty wheel also copies its neighbor when it is\n spun by steps, no matter the amount or the direction of the steps.\n
comment12.target=void leftyShouldSpinNormallyWithoutLeftNeighbor()
comment12.text=\n Verifies that a lefty wheel without a wheel on its left (it is the\n first one) spins like a normal wheel.\n
comment13.target=void leftyShouldCopyItsNeighborWhenAllWheelsSpin()
comment13.text=\n Verifies that when all the wheels are spun, a lefty wheel copies\n the symbol its neighbor has after that neighbor's own spin.\n
comment14.target=void leftyShouldCopyItsNewNeighborAfterSwap()
comment14.text=\n Verifies that a lefty wheel follows the wheel that is on its left\n at the moment of the spin, even after the wheels were swapped.\n
comment15.target=void rebelShouldNotBeLocked()
comment15.text=\n Verifies that a rebel wheel doesn't let itself be locked\: the\n operation fails and the wheel stays unlocked.\n
comment16.target=void rebelShouldNotBeSwapped()
comment16.text=\n Verifies that a rebel wheel doesn't let itself be swapped, whether\n it is given as the first or as the second wheel of the swap.\n
comment17.target=void rebelShouldNotBeRemoved()
comment17.text=\n Verifies that a rebel wheel doesn't let itself be removed.\n
comment18.target=void rebelShouldStillSpinAndPlaceSymbols()
comment18.text=\n Verifies that a rebel wheel can still be spun and have a symbol\n placed, like a normal wheel.\n
comment19.target=void normalWheelsNextToARebelShouldStillBeLockedSwappedAndRemoved()
comment19.text=\n Verifies that the restrictions of a rebel wheel don't affect the\n normal wheels next to it.\n
comment2.target=void setUp()
comment2.text=\n Sets up the test fixture.\n\n Called before every test case method.\n
comment20.target=void ephemeralShouldNeverFailNoMatterHowManyTimesItShrinks()
comment20.text=\n Verifies that an ephemeral symbol can shrink as many times as\n needed without failing\: it stops at a point and never reaches a\n size of zero, which the figure doesn't accept.\n
comment21.target=void ephemeralShouldStillBeReportedAfterBecomingAPoint()
comment21.text=\n Verifies that a wheel whose only symbol is ephemeral can be spun\n well past the moment the symbol becomes a point, and that the\n symbol is still the one the wheel reports.\n
comment22.target=void ephemeralShouldKeepItsPlaceInTheWheelWhileItShrinks()
comment22.text=\n Verifies that an ephemeral symbol keeps its place in the cycle of\n the wheel while it shrinks\: the wheel goes through its symbols in\n the same order as always.\n
comment23.target=void shrunkEphemeralShouldStillCountForJackpot()
comment23.text=\n Verifies that an ephemeral symbol that has become a point still\n counts for the distinct symbols and for the jackpot.\n
comment24.target=void ephemeralShouldNotChangeTheRulesOfALockedWheel()
comment24.text=\n Verifies that an ephemeral symbol doesn't make a spin on a locked\n wheel succeed\: the spin is still rejected.\n
comment25.target=void shyShouldNeverFailNoMatterHowManyTimesItIsSelected()
comment25.text=\n Verifies that a shy symbol can be selected over and over without\n failing, whether or not its figure is on screen.\n
comment26.target=void shyShouldBeReportedEveryTimeItIsSelectedBySpinning()
comment26.text=\n Verifies that every time the wheel stops at a shy symbol, hidden\n or not, the wheel reports it as its current symbol.\n
comment27.target=void shyShouldBeReportedEveryTimeItIsSelectedByPlacingIt()
comment27.text=\n Verifies that a shy symbol can also be selected with placeSymbol\n as many times as wanted.\n
comment28.target=void hiddenShyShouldStillCountForConfigurationAndJackpot()
comment28.text=\n Verifies that hiding is only visual\: a shy symbol selected for the\n first time (so it is hidden) is still the one its wheel reports,\n and it counts for the distinct symbols and for the jackpot.\n
comment29.target=void lazyShouldOnlyAdvanceEveryOtherSpin()
comment29.text=\n Verifies that a lazy wheel only answers to every other spin\: it\n advances with the first one, ignores the second one, advances with\n the third one, and so on. An ignored spin is not an error.\n
comment3.target=void shouldAddEveryTypeOfWheel()
comment3.text=\n Verifies that addWheel(type, pos) creates a wheel of the class that\n matches every offered type, and that null or "" create a normal one.\n
comment30.target=void lazyShouldSkipHalfOfTheStepsWhenSpunBySteps()
comment30.text=\n Verifies that a lazy wheel spun by steps only advances with the\n odd steps\: with 3 steps it moves 2 positions.\n
comment31.target=void lazyShouldAlwaysAcceptAPlacedSymbol()
comment31.text=\n Verifies that a lazy wheel doesn't refuse a placeSymbol\: it is only\n lazy with the spins.\n
comment32.target=void dizzyShouldNeverFailNoMatterHowManyTimesItFlips()
comment32.text=\n Verifies that a dizzy symbol can flip over and over without\n failing.\n
comment33.target=void dizzyShouldKeepItsPlaceInTheWheelWhileItFlips()
comment33.text=\n Verifies that a dizzy symbol keeps its place in the cycle of the\n wheel while it flips on every spin.\n
comment34.target=void dizzyShouldStillCountForJackpot()
comment34.text=\n Verifies that a dizzy symbol, flipped or not, still counts for the\n jackpot.\n
comment35.target=void wheelShouldCycleThroughSymbolsOfEveryType()
comment35.text=\n Verifies that a wheel with one symbol of every type goes through\n all of them in order, like a wheel of normal symbols.\n
comment36.target=void specialWheelsShouldWorkWithSpecialSymbols()
comment36.text=\n Verifies that the special wheels work with special symbols\: a\n lazy wheel still skips every other spin and a lefty wheel still\n copies its neighbor, even when the symbol is shy.\n
comment37.target=void shouldDeleteASymbolOfASpecialType()
comment37.text=\n Verifies that a symbol of a special type can be deleted like any\n other, from the catalog and from the wheels.\n
comment38.target=void normalSymbolShouldNeverChange()
comment38.text=\n Verifies that a normal symbol never changes its size nor hides,\n no matter how many times its wheel spins.\n
comment39.target=void ephemeralShouldShrinkOnEverySpinUntilItIsAPoint()
comment39.text=\n Verifies that an ephemeral symbol shrinks one step on every spin of\n its wheel until it becomes a point, and then stays that size.\n
comment4.target=void shouldAddWheelIgnoringCaseAndSpacesOfTheType()
comment4.text=\n Verifies that the type of a wheel is not case sensitive and ignores\n surrounding spaces.\n
comment40.target=void ephemeralShouldShrinkOnALeftyWheelThatCopiesItsNeighbor()
comment40.text=\n Verifies that an ephemeral symbol on a lefty wheel also shrinks when\n the wheel spins by copying its left neighbor.\n
comment41.target=void ephemeralShouldShrinkOncePerStep()
comment41.text=\n Verifies that an ephemeral symbol shrinks once per step when its\n wheel is spun by steps.\n
comment42.target=void shyShouldAlternateBetweenHiddenAndVisibleEveryTimeItIsSelected()
comment42.text=\n Verifies that a shy symbol hides the first time it is selected and\n shows itself again the second time, both when it is placed and when\n the wheel stops at it after a spin.\n
comment43.target=void shyShouldCountEveryStepThatStopsAtItWhenSpunBySteps()
comment43.text=\n Verifies that, when a wheel is spun by steps, a step that stops at a\n shy symbol counts as a selection even if the wheel keeps going.\n
comment44.target=void dizzyShouldFlipOnEverySpin()
comment44.text=\n Verifies that a dizzy symbol flips upside down on every spin of its\n wheel and gets back to its normal position on the next one.\n
comment45.target=void lazyShouldNotNotifyItsSymbolsWhenItIgnoresASpin()
comment45.text=\n Verifies that a lazy wheel doesn't tell its symbols about a spin it\n ignores\: an ephemeral symbol only shrinks on the spins the wheel\n answers to.\n
comment46.target=void shyShouldToggleOnALeftyWheelEveryTimeItIsCopied()
comment46.text=\n Verifies that a shy symbol on a lefty wheel counts as selected every\n time the lefty copies it from its neighbor.\n
comment47.target=void tearDown()
comment47.text=\n Tears down the test fixture.\n\n Called after every test case method.\n
comment5.target=void shouldNotAddWheelOfUnknownType()
comment5.text=\n Verifies that an unknown type of wheel adds nothing and sets the\n machine status to not ok.\n
comment6.target=void shouldAddEveryTypeOfSymbol()
comment6.text=\n Verifies that addSymbol(type, pos, color) registers in the catalog\n a symbol of the class that matches every offered type.\n
comment7.target=void shouldNotAddSymbolOfUnknownType()
comment7.text=\n Verifies that an unknown type of symbol adds nothing and sets the\n machine status to not ok.\n
comment8.target=void shouldNotAddSameColorWithAnotherType()
comment8.text=\n Verifies that a color can't be registered twice, even if the second\n time it is given with a different type.\n
comment9.target=void shouldGiveSpecialSymbolsToEveryWheel()
comment9.text=\n Verifies that a symbol of a special type reaches every wheel,\n whether the wheel was created before or after the symbol.\n
numComments=48
